    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Examples from a high quality 3D data set are presented in order to test the effectiveness of fault mapping from computed seismic attribute maps. It is demonstrated that these maps can give a more precise indication of the spatial distribution of faults than time slices. The method is quicker than detailed interpretation and cross correlation between lines. It may have some potential in the prediction of sub-seismic faulting.",
